their populations at the last survey (or by their number of populations without
\code{abundance}). \code{slope_min} and \code{slope_max} are the smallest and largest slope among species.
Means and variances are those of the measured individuals, so they include sampling error,
as field data would; \code{\link[=subsample_individuals]{subsample_individuals()}} changes the effort.
